.SH "DDC Query Language Documentation"
.IX Header "DDC Query Language Documentation"
.SS "Overview"
.IX Subsection "Overview"
This documentation describes the query language accepted by
\&\s-1DDC\s0 version 2.0.23.  Current sources for \s-1DDC\s0 should be available
from
http://sourceforge.net/projects/ddc\-concordance.
.PP
The \s-1DDC\s0 query parsing, compilation, and evaluation code was
re-written for version 2.0.  The new query parser should be
largely compatible with older \s-1DDC\s0 versions; incompatibilities are
due to new query sub-types (e.g.
value sets,
term expansion pipelines,
count-queries)
and/or bugfixes (symbol and regex escapes, quoted symbols, etc.).
Documentation for the legacy \s-1DDC\s0 query language can be found with
the source or on the web at
http://odo.dwds.de/~moocow/software/ddc/DDCReadme.pdf.
.PP
The grammar below is given in a subset of standard
\&\s-1BNF\s0 notation
using only the choice (\*(L"|\*(R") and termination (\*(L";\*(R") operators.
Where available, nonterminal symbols on the right-hand side of grammar rules
appear as
italicized lower-case hyperlinks.
Literal terminal symbols are typeset in green monospace,
and special terminal symbols appear as
\&\s-1ITALICIZED\s0 UPPER-CASE \s-1HYPERLINKS\s0.
Comments may appear after each rule in C notation
/* like this */.
.SS "Grammar Rules"
.IX Subsection "Grammar Rules"
\fITop-Level Rule(s)\fR
.IX Subsection "Top-Level Rule(s)"
.PP
.Vb 4
\& query ::=                   /*\-\- Top\-level rule (query root) \-\-*/
\&           query_conditions  /* Traditional context\-query */
\&         | count_query       /* Count\-query (histogram data) */
\&         ;
.Ve
.PP
\fIContext Query Rules\fR
.IX Subsection "Context Query Rules"
.PP
.Vb 3
\& query_conditions ::=                                                       /*\-\- Top\-level context\-query root \-\-*/
\&                      q_clause q_filters                                    /* Filters may be empty */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& q_clause         ::=                                                       /*\-\- Main query clause (logical operations) \-\-*/
\&                      qc_basic                                              /* Single\-condition clause */
\&                    | qc_boolean                                            /* Complex boolean condition */
\&                    | qc_concat                                             /* Concatenated query clauses (implicit logical conjunction) */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qc_basic         ::=                                                       /*\-\- Basic query clause (single logical condition) \-\-*/
\&                      qc_tokens                                             /* Phrase or single\-token condition */
\&                    | qc_near                                               /* Unordered proximity constraint */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qc_boolean       ::=                                                       /*\-\- Boolean combination of query conditions \-\-*/
\&                      q_clause && q_clause                                  /* Logical conjunction (\*(Aqand\*(Aq) */
\&                    | q_clause || q_clause                                  /* Logical disjunction (\*(Aqor\*(Aq) */
\&                    | ! q_clause                                            /* Logical negation (\*(Aqnot\*(Aq): not be interpretable for all clauses */
\&                    | ( qc_boolean )                                        /* Explicit grouping */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qc_concat        ::=                                                       /*\-\- Implicit conjunction of multiple independent query clauses (ddc >= v2.0.20) \-\-*/
\&                      qc_basic qc_basic                                     /* ... only basic query clauses can be implicitly conjoined */
\&                    | qc_concat qc_basic                                    /* ... arbitrarily many clauses may be added */
\&                    | ( qc_concat )                                         /* ... explicit grouping is allowed */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qc_near          ::=                                                       /*\-\- Unordered proximity constraint \-\-*/
\&                      NEAR ( qc_tokens , qc_tokens , integer )              /* ... over 2 argument conditions */
\&                    | NEAR ( qc_tokens , qc_tokens , qc_tokens , integer )  /* ... over 3 argument conditions */
\&                    | ( qc_near )                                           /* Explicit grouping (vacuous) */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qc_tokens        ::=                                                       /*\-\- Phrase or single\-token condition \-\-*/
\&                      qc_word                                               /* Single\-token condition */
\&                    | qc_phrase                                             /* Ordered sequence of single\-token conditions */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qc_phrase        ::=                                                       /*\-\- Ordered sequence of single\-token conditions \-\-*/
\&                      " l_phrase "                                          /* Phrases are enclosed in double\-quotes */
\&                    | ( qc_phrase )                                         /* Explicit grouping (vacuous) */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qc_word          ::=                                                       /*\-\- Single\-token condition \-\-*/
\&                      qw_bareword                                           /* Bareword query (expanded) */
\&                    | qw_exact                                              /* Exact match (not expanded) */
\&                    | qw_regex                                              /* Regular expression */
\&                    | qw_any                                                /* Universal match (arbitrary value) */
\&                    | qw_set_infl                                           /* Disjunction over a set of targets (expanded) */
\&                    | qw_set_exact                                          /* Disjunction over a set of literals (not expanded) */
\&                    | qw_prefix                                             /* Right\-truncated string (prefix condition) */
\&                    | qw_prefix_set                                         /* Disjunction over right\-truncated strings (prefix\-set condition) */
\&                    | qw_suffix                                             /* Left\-truncated string (suffix condition) */
\&                    | qw_suffix_set                                         /* Disjunction over left\-truncated strings (suffix\-set condition) */
\&                    | qw_infix                                              /* Substring (infix) condition */
\&                    | qw_infix_set                                          /* Disjunction over substrings (infix\-set condition) */
\&                    | qw_thesaurus                                          /* Thesaurus condition (\*(AqThes\*(Aq index) */
\&                    | qw_morph                                              /* Morphological property condition (\*(AqMorphPattern\*(Aq index) */
\&                    | qw_lemma                                              /* Lemma property condition (\*(AqLemma\*(Aq index) */
\&                    | qw_chunk                                              /* Syntactic property condition (\*(AqChunk\*(Aq index) */
\&                    | qw_anchor                                             /* Position in segment (a.k.a. \*(Aqbreak collection\*(Aq) */
\&                    | qw_listfile                                           /* Disjunction over values (lines) read from a server\-side file (command\-line only) */
\&                    | qw_with                                               /* Conjunction of multiple conditions on a single token */
\&                    | ( qc_word )                                           /* Explicit grouping (e.g. for WITH, expanders, etc.) */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_bareword      ::=                                                       /*\-\- String match condition with implicit term expansion \-\-*/
\&                      s_word l_txchain                                      /* ... on \*(AqToken\*(Aq index, with optional expansion pipeline */
\&                    | s_index = s_word l_txchain                            /* ... on user\-specified index, with optional expansion pipeline */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_exact         ::=                                                       /*\-\- Literal string match condition \-\-*/
\&                      @ s_word                                              /* ... on \*(AqToken\*(Aq index */
\&                    | s_index = @ s_word                                    /* ... or on user\-specified index */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_regex         ::=                                                       /*\-\- Regular expression match using perl syntax \-\-*/
\&                      regex                                                 /* ... on \*(AqToken\*(Aq index */
\&                    | s_index = regex                                       /* ... on user\-specified index */
\&                    | neg_regex                                             /* ... on \*(AqToken\*(Aq index, negated */
\&                    | s_index = neg_regex                                   /* ... on user\-specified index, negated */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_any           ::=                                                       /*\-\- Universal match (aka wildcard token) \-\-*/
\&                      *                                                     /* ... on \*(AqToken\*(Aq index */
\&                    | s_index = *                                           /* ... on user\-specified index (vacuous; index name is ignored) */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_set_infl      ::=                                                       /*\-\- Disjunction over a set of (expanded) target values \-\-*/
\&                      { l_set } l_txchain                                   /* ... in \*(AqToken\*(Aq index, with optional expansion pipeline */
\&                    | s_index = { l_set } l_txchain                         /* ... in user\-specified index, with optional expansion pipeline */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_set_exact     ::=                                                       /*\-\- Disjunction over a set of literal values \-\-*/
\&                      @{ l_set }                                            /* ... in the \*(AqToken\*(Aq index */
\&                    | s_index = @{ l_set }                                  /* ... in a user\-specified index */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_prefix        ::=                                                       /*\-\- Right\-truncated string (prefix condition) \-\-*/
\&                      s_prefix                                              /* ... on \*(AqToken\*(Aq index */
\&                    | s_index = s_prefix                                    /* ... on user\-specified index */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_prefix_set    ::=                                                       /*\-\- Disjunction over right\-truncated strings (prefix\-set condition) \-\-*/
\&                      { l_set }*                                            /* ... on \*(AqToken\*(Aq index */
\&                    | s_index = { l_set }*                                  /* ... on user\-specified index */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_suffix        ::=                                                       /*\-\- Left\-truncated string (suffix condition) \-\-*/
\&                      s_suffix                                              /* ... on \*(AqToken\*(Aq index */
\&                    | s_index = s_suffix                                    /* ... on user\-specified index */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_suffix_set    ::=                                                       /*\-\- Disjunction over left\-truncated strings (suffix\-set condition) \-\-*/
\&                      *{ l_set }                                            /* ... on \*(AqToken\*(Aq index */
\&                    | s_index = *{ l_set }                                  /* ... on user\-specified index */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_infix         ::=                                                       /*\-\- Substring (infix) condition \-\-*/
\&                      s_infix                                               /* ... on \*(AqToken\*(Aq index */
\&                    | s_index = s_infix                                     /* ... on user\-specified index */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_infix_set     ::=                                                       /*\-\- Disjunction over substrings (infix set) \-\-*/
\&                      *{ l_set }*                                           /* ... on \*(AqToken\*(Aq index */
\&                    | s_index = *{ l_set }*                                 /* ... on user\-specified index */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_thesaurus     ::=                                                       /*\-\- Thesaurus condition (SYNTAX CHANGED!) \-\-*/
\&                      :{ s_semclass }                                       /* ... on \*(AqThes\*(Aq index */
\&                    | s_index = :{ s_semclass }                             /* ... on user\-specified index */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_morph         ::=                                                       /*\-\- Morphological property condition \-\-*/
\&                      [ l_morph ]                                           /* ... on \*(AqMorphPattern\*(Aq index */
\&                    | s_index = [ l_morph ]                                 /* ... on user\-specified index */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_lemma         ::=                                                       /*\-\- Lemma property condition (not for D* corpora) \-\-*/
\&                      % s_lemma                                             /* ... on \*(AqLemma\*(Aq index */
\&                    | s_index = % s_lemma                                   /* ... on user\-specified index */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_chunk         ::=                                                       /*\-\- Syntactic property condition \-\-*/
\&                      ^ s_chunk                                             /* ... on \*(AqChunk\*(Aq index */
\&                    | s_index = ^ s_chunk                                   /* ... on user\-specified index */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_anchor        ::=                                                       /*\-\- Position in segment (a.k.a. \*(Aqbreak collection\*(Aq) \-\-*/
\&                      $. = int_str                                          /* ... in \*(Aqs\*(Aq collection (0:initial, \-1:final) */
\&                    | $. s_break = int_str                                  /* ... in user\-specified break collection */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_listfile      ::=                                                       /*\-\- Disjunction over values read from a server\-side file (command\-line only) \-\-*/
\&                      < s_filename                                          /* ... on \*(AqToken\*(Aq index */
\&                    | s_index = < s_filename                                /* ... on user\-specified index */
\&                    ;
\& 
\& qw_with          ::=                                                       /*\-\- Conjunction of multiple conditions over a single token \-\-*/
\&                      qc_word WITH qc_word                                  /* ... note that negated conditions are not admissable here */
\&                    ;
.Ve
.PP
\fIQuery Filter Rules\fR
.IX Subsection "Query Filter Rules"
.PP
.Vb 5
\& q_filters       ::=                                   /*\-\- List of global query options \-\-*/
\&                                                       /* empty */
\&                   | q_filters q_flag                  /* ... query flag */
\&                   | q_filters q_filter                /* ... query filter */
\&                   ;
\& 
\& q_flag          ::=                                   /*\-\- Global query flags \-\-*/
\&                     : qf_subcorpora                   /* subcorporus selection */
\&                   | #CNTXT integer                    /* hit context window (number of sentences; alias: #N) */
\&                   | #WITHIN symbol                    /* hit container type (e.g. \*(Aqfile\*(Aq; alias: #IN) */
\&                   | #SEPARATE_HITS                    /* return each match as a separate hit (aliases: #SEPARATE, #SEP, #NOJOIN_HITS, #NOJOIN) */
\&                   | #JOIN_HITS                        /* return at most one hit for each container selected by #WITHIN (default, aliases: #JOIN, #NOSEPARATE_HITS, #NOSEPARATE, #NOSEP) */
\&                   | #FILENAMES                        /* request filenames in output metadata */
\&                   | ! #FILENAMES                      /* ... or disable filenames in output metadata */
\&                   | #DEBUG_RANK                       /* request verbose rank debugging in output metadata */
\&                   | ! #DEBUG_RANK                     /* ... or disable verbose rank debugging */
\&                   ;
\& 
\& q_filter        ::=                                   /*\-\- Global query selection and/or sort filter \-\-*/
\&                     qf_has_field                      /* restrict hits based on document metadata */
\&                   | qf_rank_sort                      /* ... sort hits by TF\-IDF rank */
\&                   | qf_context_sort                   /* ... sort hits lexicographically by context */
\&                   | qf_size_sort                      /* ... sort/filter hits by (sentence) length */
\&                   | qf_date_sort                      /* ... sort/filter hits by document date */
\&                   | qf_bibl_sort                      /* ... sort/filter hits by document metadata */
\&                   | qf_random_sort                    /* ... sort hits pseudo\-randomly */
\&                   ;
\& 
\& qf_has_field    ::=                                   /*\-\- Metadata restriction (alias: #HAS_FIELD) \-\-*/
\&                     #HAS [ s_xfield , symbol ]        /* ... literal match */
\&                   | #HAS [ s_xfield , regex ]         /* ... regular expression match */
\&                   | #HAS [ s_xfield , neg_regex ]     /* ... negated regular expression match */
\&                   | #HAS [ s_xfield , s_prefix ]      /* ... prefix match */
\&                   | #HAS [ s_xfield , s_suffix ]      /* ... suffix match */
\&                   | #HAS [ s_xfield , s_infix ]       /* ... infix match */
\&                   | #HAS [ s_xfield , { l_set } ]     /* ... disjunction over a set of target values */
\&                   | ! qf_has_field                    /* ... negated filter expression */
\&                   ;
\& 
\& qf_rank_sort    ::=                                   /*\-\- Sort hits by TF\-IDF rank \-\-*/
\&                     #GREATER_BY_RANK                  /* ... in descending order (aliases: #DESC_RANK, #DESC_BY_RANK) */
\&                   | #LESS_BY_RANK                     /* ... in ascending order (aliases: #ASC_RANK, #ASC_BY_RANK) */
\&                   ;
\& 
\& qf_context_sort ::=                                   /*\-\- Sort and/or filter hits lexicographically by context (required Bigrams index prior to ddc v2.0.19) \-\-*/
\&                     #LESS_BY_MIDDLE qfb_ctxsort       /* ... in ascending order by user\-specified offset relative to hit center (default offset=0; aliases: #MID, #MIDDLE, #ASC_MIDDLE, ...) */
\&                   | #GREATER_BY_MIDDLE qfb_ctxsort    /* ... in descending order by user\-specified offset relative to hit center (default offset=0; aliases: #DESC_MIDDLE, #DESC_BY_MIDDLE, ...) */
\&                   | #LESS_BY_LEFT qfb_ctxsort         /* ... in ascending order by preceding context (default offset=\-1; aliases: #LEFT, #ASC_LEFT, #ASC_BY_LEFT, ...) */
\&                   | #GREATER_BY_LEFT qfb_ctxsort      /* ... in descending order by preceding context (default offset=\-1; aliases: #DESC_LEFT, #DESC_BY_LEFT, ....) */
\&                   | #LESS_BY_RIGHT qfb_ctxsort        /* ... in ascending order by following context (default offset=1; aliases: #RIGHT, #ASC_RIGHT, ...) */
\&                   | #GREATER_BY_RIGHT qfb_ctxsort     /* ... in descending order by following context (default offset=1; aliases: #DESC_RIGHT, #DESC_BY_RIGHT, ...) */
\&                   ;
\& 
\& qf_size_sort    ::=                                   /*\-\- Sort or filter hits by (sentence) length \-\-*/
\&                     #LESS_BY_SIZE qfb_int             /* ... in ascending order, with optional bounds (aliases: #ASC_SIZE, #ASC_BY_SIZE) */
\&                   | #GREATER_BY_SIZE qfb_int          /* ... in descending order, with optional bounds (aliases: #DESC_SIZE, #DESC_BY_SIZE) */
\&                   | #SIZE [ int_str ]                 /* ... restricted to specified size (aliases: #IS_SIZE, #HAS_SIZE) */
\&                   ;
\& 
\& qf_date_sort    ::=                                   /*\-\- Sort or filter hits by document date \-\-*/
\&                     #LESS_BY_DATE qfb_date            /* ... in ascending order, with optional bounds (aliases: #ASC_DATE, #ASC_BY_DATE) */
\&                   | #GREATER_BY_DATE qfb_date         /* ... in descending order, with optional bounds (aliases: #DESC_DATE, #DESC_BY_DATE) */
\&                   | #DATE [ date ]                    /* ... restricted to specified date (aliases: #IS_DATE, #HAS_DATE) */
\&                   ;
\& 
\& qf_bibl_sort    ::=                                   /*\-\- Sort or filter hits by document metadata \-\-*/
\&                     #LESS_BY [ s_field qfb_bibl ]     /* ... in ascending order, with optional bounds (aliases: #ASC, #ASC_BY) */
\&                   | #GREATER_BY [ s_field qfb_bibl ]  /* ... in descending order, with optional bounds (aliases: #DESC, #DESC_BY) */
\&                   ;
\& 
\& qf_random_sort  ::=                                   /*\-\- Sort hits pseudo\-randomly (alias: #RAND) \-\-*/
\&                     #RANDOM                           /* ... with an implicit seed of 0 (zero) */
\&                   | #RANDOM [ ]                       /* ... with an implicit seed of 0 (zero) */
\&                   | #RANDOM [ int_str ]               /* ... with a user\-specified random seed */
\&                   ;
\& 
\& qfb_int         ::=                                   /*\-\- Optional integer bounds for query filters \-\-*/
\&                                                       /* ... empty (full range) */
\&                   | [ ]                               /* ... empty brackets (full range) */
\&                   | [ int_str ]                       /* ... lower bound only */
\&                   | [ int_str , ]                     /* ... lower bound only */
\&                   | [ int_str , int_str ]             /* ... lower bound, upper bound */
\&                   | [ , int_str ]                     /* ... upper bound only */
\&                   ;
\& 
\& qfb_date        ::=                                   /*\-\- Optional date bounds for query filters \-\-*/
\&                                                       /* ... empty (full range) */
\&                   | [ ]                               /* ... empty brackets (full range) */
\&                   | [ date ]                          /* ... lower bound only */
\&                   | [ date , ]                        /* ... lower bound only */
\&                   | [ date , date ]                   /* ... lower bound, upper bound */
\&                   | [ , date ]                        /* ... upper bound only */
\&                   ;
\& 
\& qfb_bibl        ::=                                   /*\-\- Optional string metadata bounds for query filters \-\-*/
\&                                                       /* ... empty (full range) */
\&                   | ,                                 /* ... empty (full range) */
\&                   | , ,                               /* ... empty (full range) */
\&                   | , symbol                          /* ... lower bound only */
\&                   | , symbol ,                        /* ... lower bound only */
\&                   | , , symbol                        /* ... upper bound only */
\&                   | , symbol , symbol                 /* ... lower bound, upper bound */
\&                   ;
\& 
\& qfb_ctxsort     ::=                                   /*\-\- Optional sort\-key attribute, offset, and/or bounds for context\-sort operators \-\-*/
\&                     [ qfb_ctxkey ]                    /* ... given key (full range) */
\&                   | [ qfb_bibl ]                      /* ... given range (Token attribute, zero offset) */
\&                   | [ qfb_ctxkey qfb_bibl ]           /* ... given key and range */
\&                   ;
\& 
\& qfb_ctxkey      ::=                                   /*\-\- Optional sort\-key attribute and/or offset for context\-sort operators \-\-*/
\&                     sym_str                           /* ... given attribute (zero offset) */
\&                   | integer                           /* ... given offset (Token attribute) */
\&                   | sym_str integer                   /* ... given attribute and offset */
\&                   ;
.Ve
.PP
\fICount-Query Rules\fR
.IX Subsection "Count-Query Rules"
.PP
.Vb 3
\& count_query   ::=                                           /*\-\- Top\-level count\-query root \-\-*/
\&                   COUNT ( query_conditions ) count_filters  /* Filters may be empty */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& count_filters ::=                                           /*\-\- List of count\-query options \-\-*/
\&                                                             /* empty */
\&                 | count_filters count_filter                /* non\-empty */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& count_filter  ::=                                           /*\-\- Single count\-query option \-\-*/
\&                   count_by                                  /* histogram bin selection */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& count_by      ::=                                           /*\-\- Select count\-query histogram keys (metadata tuples) \-\-*/
\&                   BY l_countkeys                            /* SQL\-style syntax */
\&                 | BY [ l_countkeys ]                        /* DDC filter\-style syntax */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& l_countkeys   ::=                                           /*\-\- Tuple of bibliographic metadata fields \-\-*/
\&                                                             /* ... empty */
\&                 | l_countkeys ,                             /* ... comma\-separated */
\&                 | l_countkeys count_key                     /* ... or space\-separated */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& count_key     ::=                                           /*\-\- Histogram bin component \-\-*/
\&                   *                                         /* ... constant string \*(Aq*\*(Aq (global counts only) */
\&                 | @ symbol                                  /* ... constant user\-defined string */
\&                 | FILEID                                    /* ... subcorpus\-local file\-id (integer) */
\&                 | FILENAME                                  /* ... filename */
\&                 | DATE                                      /* ... date string (YYYY\-MM\-DD) */
\&                 | DATE / i_slice                            /* ... date slice, computed as (i_slice*int(year/i_slice)) */
\&                 | s_field                                   /* ... bibliographic string\-field value (e.g. textClass) */
\&                 | count_key ~ replace_regex                 /* ... on\-the\-fly regex transformation (can be chained) */
\&                 | ( count_key )                             /* ... explicit grouping */
\&                 ;
.Ve
.PP
\fIList-like Constituents\fR
.IX Subsection "List-like Constituents"
.PP
.Vb 5
\& l_set         ::=                              /*\-\- Set of string values \-\-*/
\&                                                /* empty set */
\&                 | l_set s_word                 /* ... set elements are separated by whitespace */
\&                 | l_set ,                      /* ... or by commas */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& l_morph       ::=                              /*\-\- List of morphological properties (should match index) \-\-*/
\&                                                /* empty list */
\&                 | l_morph s_morphitem          /* ... list elements are separated by whitespace */
\&                 | l_morph ,                    /* ... or commas */
\&                 | l_morph ;                    /* ... or semicolons (for compatibility) */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& l_phrase      ::=                              /*\-\- Ordered sequence of single\-word conditions with optional proximity constraints \-\-*/
\&                   qc_word                      /* Singleton phrase */
\&                 | l_phrase qc_word             /* ... phrase elements are separated by whitespace */
\&                 | l_phrase #< integer qc_word  /* ... allowing at most N intervening tokens (default=\*(Aq#<0\*(Aq: immediate successor) */
\&                 | l_phrase #> integer qc_word  /* ... requiring at least N intervening tokens */
\&                 | l_phrase #= integer qc_word  /* ... allowing exactly N intervening tokens */
\&                 | l_phrase # integer qc_word   /* ... backwards\-compatible #N is an alias for #<N */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& l_txchain     ::=                              /*\-\- Term expansion pipeline \-\-*/
\&                                                /* Empty pipeline or \*(Aq|\-\*(Aq uses index\-dependent default aka \*(Aq|INDEX\*(Aq */
\&                 | l_txchain s_expander         /* ... pipeline concatenation \*(Aq|Expander1 |Expander2 |...\*(Aq */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& qf_subcorpora ::=                              /*\-\- Set of target subcorpora \-\-*/
\&                                                /* ... empty subcorpus set */
\&                 | s_subcorpus                  /* ... singleton subcorpus (symbol) */
\&                 | qf_subcorpora , s_subcorpus  /* ... multiple subcorpora are separated by commas */
\&                 ;
.Ve
.PP
\fIPreterminals and Aliases\fR
.IX Subsection "Preterminals and Aliases"
.PP
.Vb 4
\& s_index       ::=                              /*\-\- Index name (must be defined in .opt file) \-\-*/
\&                   $                            /* Bare dollar uses query\-type default (usually \*(AqToken\*(Aq) */
\&                 | $ symbol                     /* Explicit index name */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& s_word        ::=                              /*\-\- A single word or string value \-\-*/
\&                   symbol                       /* ... can be any symbol */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& s_semclass    ::=                              /*\-\- Semantic class used by :{...} queries \-\-*/
\&                   symbol                       /* ... can be any symbol */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& s_lemma       ::=                              /*\-\- Lemma used by %L queries \-\-*/
\&                   symbol                       /* ... can be any symbol */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& s_chunk       ::=                              /*\-\- Chunk name used by ^C queries \-\-*/
\&                   symbol                       /* ... can be any symbol */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& s_break       ::=                              /*\-\- Break collection name used by $. queries \-\-*/
\&                   symbol                       /* ... can be any symbol (but must be defined in .opt file) */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& s_filename    ::=                              /*\-\- Filename used by <F queries \-\-*/
\&                   symbol                       /* ... can be any symbol (server\-side filename) */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& s_morphitem   ::=                              /*\-\- Morphological property used by [...] queries \-\-*/
\&                   symbol                       /* ... can be any symbol */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& symbol        ::=                              /*\-\- User\-specified symbol or string \-\-*/
\&                   SYMBOL                       /* Bareword or single\-quoted string with C\-style escapes */
\&                 | INTEGER                      /* ... every decimal number is also a valid symbol */
\&                 | DATE                         /* ... every date\-string is also a valid symbol */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& sym_str       ::=                              /*\-\- User\-specified string symbol \-\-*/
\&                   SYMBOL                       /* ... cannot be an integer or date */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& s_prefix      ::=                              /*\-\- Prefix condition string \-\-*/
\&                   PREFIX                       /* ... ends with a literal \*(Aq*\*(Aq */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& s_suffix      ::=                              /*\-\- Suffix condition string \-\-*/
\&                   SUFFIX                       /* ... begins with a literal \*(Aq*\*(Aq */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& s_infix       ::=                              /*\-\- Infix condition string \-\-*/
\&                   INFIX                        /* ... begins and ends with literal \*(Aq*\*(Aq */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& s_expander    ::=                              /*\-\- Term expander label \-\-*/
\&                   EXPANDER                     /* ... begins with a literal \*(Aq|\*(Aq, and may be \*(Aq|\-\*(Aq for an index\-dependent default */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& s_subcorpus   ::=                              /*\-\- Named subcorpus used by :... filter \-\-*/
\&                   symbol                       /* ... can be any symbol */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& s_field       ::=                              /*\-\- Document metadata field name \-\-*/
\&                   symbol                       /* ... is just a symbol */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& s_fieldval    ::=                              /*\-\- Document metadata field value \-\-*/
\&                   symbol                       /* ... is just a symbol */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& s_xfield      ::=                              /*\-\- Document metadata field name or pseudo\-field \-\-*/
\&                   symbol                       /* ... is just a symbol */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& regex         ::=                              /*\-\- Regular expressions \-\-*/
\&                   REGEX                        /* ... are slash\-delimited in perl syntax */
\&                 | REGEX REGOPT                 /* ... with optional modifiers (gimsx) */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& neg_regex     ::=                              /*\-\- Negated regular expressions \-\-*/
\&                   NEG_REGEX                    /* ... are slash\-delimited in perl syntax, with leading \*(Aq!\*(Aq */
\&                 | NEG_REGEX REGOPT             /* ... and with optional modifiers (gimsx) */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& replace_regex ::=                              /*\-\- On\-the\-fly regular expression search\-and\-replace \-\-*/
\&                   SEARCH_REPLACE_REGEX         /* ... are slash\-delimited in perl syntax: s/SEARCH/REPLACE/ */
\&                 | SEARCH_REPLACE_REGEX REGOPT  /* ... with optional modifiers (gimsx) */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& integer       ::=                              /*\-\- Non\-negative decimal integer \-\-*/
\&                   int_str                      /* ... parsed as an integer */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& int_str       ::=                              /*\-\- Non\-negative decimal integer \-\-*/
\&                   INTEGER                      /* ... parsed as a string */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& i_slice       ::=                              /*\-\- Date interval for histogram bins \-\-*/
\&                   integer                      /* ... is just an integer (interval size in years) */
\&                 ;
\& 
\& date          ::=                              /*\-\- date string \-\-*/
\&                   DATE                         /* ... e.g. YYYY(\-MM(\-DD)?)? */
\&                 | INTEGER                      /* ... every valid integer is also a valid date (year part only) */
\&                 ;
.Ve
.SS "Terminal Symbols"
.IX Subsection "Terminal Symbols"
\fICommon Definitions\fR
.IX Subsection "Common Definitions"
.PP
The underlying flex scanner makes use of several regular expression
\&'macros' using the notation {\s-1MACRO\s0}.
The following macros are defined for the underlying scanner:
.PP
.Vb 2
\& ws             [ \et\en\er\ef\ev]
\& punct          [\e^\e!\e~\e$\e@\e%\e/\e=\e?\e_\e:\e;\e+\e#\e.\e\e\e*\e,\e\*(Aq\e"\e&\e|\e(\e)\e[\e]\e{\e}\e<\e>]
\& 
\& symbol_cfirst  [^ \et\er\en\ef\ev\e0\e^\e&\e|\e!\e(\e)\e[\e]\e{\e}\e<\e>\e\*(Aq\e"\e,\e;\e:\e#\e=\e*\e%\e\e\e~\e/\e$\e@\e?\e_\e+\e.]
\& symbol_crest   [^ \et\er\en\ef\ev\e0\e^\e&\e|\e!\e(\e)\e[\e]\e{\e}\e<\e>\e\*(Aq\e"\e,\e;\e:\e#\e=\e*\e%\e\e\e~\e/]
\& symbol_cescape  (\e\e.)
\& symbol_text     ({symbol_cescape}|{symbol_cfirst})(({symbol_cescape}|{symbol_crest})*)
\& 
\& int_boundary   [ \et\en\er\ef\ev\e0\e^\e&\e|\e!\e(\e)\e[\e]\e{\e}\e<\e>\e\*(Aq\e"\e,\e;\e:\e#\e=\e*\e%\e~\e\e\e$\e@\e/\e?\e_\e+\e.]
\& 
\& index_name      {symbol_text}
\& 
\& sq_text         ([^\e\*(Aq]|{symbol_cescape})*
\& 
\& regex_text      ((\e\e.)|[^\e/\e\e])*
\& regex_modifier [gimsx]
.Ve
.PP
\fIQuery Keywords\fR
.IX Subsection "Query Keywords"
.PP
.Vb 10
\& (?i:near)
\& (?i:with)
\& (?i:count)
\& (?i:(file|doc)?id)
\& (?i:(file|doc)_?(name)?)
\& (?i:date)
\& (?i:\e#(cntxt|n))
\& (?i:\e#(with)?in)
\& (?i:\e#(sep(arate)?|nojoin)(_hits)?)
\& (?i:\e#(nosep(arate)?|join)(_hits)?)
\& (?i:\e#has(_field)?)
\& (?i:\e#file(_?)names)
\& (?i:\e#debug_rank)
\& (?i:\e#(greater|de?sc)(_by)?_rank)
\& (?i:\e#(less|asc)(_by)?_rank)   
\& (?i:\e#(greater|de?sc)(_by)?_date)
\& (?i:\e#(less|asc)(_by)?_date)   
\& (?i:\e#(is_|has_)?date)         
\& (?i:\e#(greater|de?sc)(_by)?_size)
\& (?i:\e#(less|asc)(_by)?_size)   
\& (?i:\e#(is_|has_)?size)         
\& (?i:\e#((less|asc)(_by)?_)?left)
\& (?i:\e#((greater|de?sc)(_by)?_)left)
\& (?i:\e#((less|asc)(_by)?_)?right)
\& (?i:\e#((greater|de?sc)(_by)?_)right)
\& (?i:\e#((less|asc)(_by)?_)?mid(dle)?)
\& (?i:\e#((greater|de?sc)(_by)?_)mid(dle)?)
\& (?i:\e#(less|asc)(_by)?)                  
\& (?i:\e#(greater|de?sc)(_by)?)   
\& (?i:\e#rand(om)?)
\& (?i:\e#by)
.Ve
.PP
The scanner supports the various reserved words used in
the query grammar.  Query keywords are matched
case-insensitively; e.g.
\&\*(L"\s-1NEAR\s0\*(R",
\&\*(L"near\*(R",
\&\*(L"Near\*(R",
and \*(L"nEaR\*(R"
are all valid instantiations of the query keyword
\&\s-1NEAR\s0.
Query keywords must be escaped if they occur anywhere
in a literal symbol, e.g. by enclosing the symbol in single quotes.
.PP
\fIRegular Expressions\fR
.IX Subsection "Regular Expressions"
.PP
.Vb 3
\&   "/"{regex_text}"/"{regex_modifier}*                  /* slash\-quoted regex, with option modifiers */
\&  "!/"{regex_text}"/"{regex_modifier}*                  /* negated regex (complement) */
\&  "s/"{regex_text}"/"{regex_text}"/"{regex_modifier}*   /* search\-and\-replace regex (for count\-by) */
.Ve
.PP
The scanner supports regular expressions enclosed by forward slashes, with
an optional suffix modifer string.  If the expression is immediately
preceded by an exclamation point (\*(L"!\*(R"), it is treated as a negated condition,
and evaluates to the complement of the set of all index items matching
the (non-negated) regular expression.
\&\s-1DDC\s0 uses \s-1PCRE\s0 as its underlying
regular expression engine, which should support the full
Perl regular expression syntax.
In particular, C\-style escapes (\*(L"\et\*(R", \*(L"\en\*(R", \*(L"\e0\*(R", etc.) and
Unicode character escapes (\*(L"\ex{17f}\*(R", \*(L"\ex{364}\*(R") may occur
within regular expressions.  Literal slashes as part of a regular expression
must be escaped with a backslash (\*(L"\e/\*(R").
The regular expression modifier \*(L"/g\*(R" (mnemonic: 'match Globally')
has a special meaning when used in \s-1DDC\s0 regex match expressions: if this modifier is set, only those index
items are retrieved which match the regular expression in the entirety;
otherwise all index items for which any substring matches the regular expression
will be retrieved.  Internally this behavior is implemented by implicitly
inserting beginning\- and end-of-string anchors into the regular expression,
thus /REGEX/g is a equivalent to /^(?:REGEX)$/.
When used in search-and-replace operations s/SEARCH/REPLACE/g, the
\&\*(L"/g\*(R" modifier causes all occurrences of the \s-1SEARCH\s0 pattern
to be replaced by the \s-1REPLACE\s0 string.
.PP
\fIPunctutation Operators and Special Characters\fR
.IX Subsection "Punctutation Operators and Special Characters"
.PP
.Vb 10
\& "&&"                           /* clause\-level conjunction operator */
\& "||"                           /* clause\-level disjunction operator */
\& "#="                           /* exact\-distance hint in phrase queries */
\& "#<"                           /* max\-distance hint for phrase queries */
\& "#>"                           /* min\-distance hint for phrase queries */
\& "$."                           /* anchor pseudo\-index (position\-index in "break collection" segment) */
\& [\e!\e.\e,\e:\e;\e$\e@\e%\e^\e#\e=\e/\e~]   /* single\-character punctuation operators */
\& [\e[\e]\e{\e}\e(\e)\e<\e>]     /* parentheses */
\& [\e"]                           /* double quotes (for pharse queries) */
\& ":{"                           /* thesaurus\-query opener */
\& "@{"                           /* literal\-set opener */
\& "*{"                           /* prefix\- or infix\-set opener */
\& "}*"                           /* suffix\-set or infix\-set closer */
\& "*"                            /* universal match wildcard */
.Ve
.PP
The scanner supports the various punctuation operators used in
the query grammar.
Punctuation operators should be escaped if they occur anywhere in a literal
symbol, e.g. by enclosing the symbol in single quotes.
.PP
\fIIntegers\fR
.IX Subsection "Integers"
.PP
.Vb 2
\& \e\*(Aq[0\-9]+\e\*(Aq                      /* single\-quoted non\-negative decimal integer */
\&   [0\-9]+/{int_boundary}         /* bareword non\-negative decimal integer */
.Ve
.PP
The scanner supports non-negative integers in decimal notation, optionally
enclosed by single quotes.  It may be necessary to introduce whitespace
or quotes in order to separate an integer token from surrounding symbols.
.PP
\fIDates\fR
.IX Subsection "Dates"
.PP
.Vb 2
\& \e\*(Aq[0\-9\e\-]+\e\*(Aq                   /* single\-quoted date\-like string */
\&   [0\-9\e\-]+/{int_boundary}      /* bareword date\-like string */
.Ve
.PP
The scanner supports date-like tokens in a superset of the \s-1ISO\s0 8601 format
(YYYY-MM-DD), optionally enclosed by single quotes.
.PP
\fISymbols and Barewords\fR
.IX Subsection "Symbols and Barewords"
.PP
.Vb 2
\& \e\*(Aq{sq_text}\e\*(Aq                   /* single\-quoted symbol */
\& {symbol_text}                  /* bareword symbol */
.Ve
.PP
Symbols (strings) are the basic building blocks of the \s-1DDC\s0 query language.
The scanner supports \*(L"bareword\*(R" symbols (e.g. my_symbol)
consisting of only alphanumeric and non-ASCII characters, underscores,
and backslash-escapes, as well as single-quoted strings
(e.g. 'symbol with whitespace'), in which only embedded quotes must be
escaped.
.PP
Escapes
.IX Subsection "Escapes"
.PP
The following special character escape sequences are supported in both bareword
and single-quoted symbols:
.PP
.Vb 12
\& Escape Description                                   
\& \ea     C\-style escape (\ex07): alert (bell)           
\& \eb     C\-style escape (\ex08): backspace              
\& \et     C\-style escape (\ex09): horizontal tab         
\& \en     C\-style escape (\ex0a): newline                
\& \ev     C\-style escape (\ex0b): vertical tab           
\& \ef     C\-style escape (\ex0c): form feed              
\& \er     C\-style escape (\ex0d): carriage return        
\& \eOOO   C\-style octal escape (byte); e.g. \e101        
\& \exXX   C\-style hexidecimal escape (byte); e.g. \ex42  
\& \euXXXX JSON\-style Unicode escape (UTF\-8); e.g. \eu0043
\& \ec     Escaped character \*(Aqc\*(Aq; e.g. \e\e
.Ve
.PP
\fITruncated Symbols\fR
.IX Subsection "Truncated Symbols"
.PP
.Vb 3
\& "*"\e\*(Aq{sq_text}\e\*(Aq"*"    /* dual\-truncated quoted string (infix symbol) */
\&    \e\*(Aq{sq_text}\e\*(Aq"*"    /* right\-truncated quoted string (prefix symbol) */
\& "*"\e\*(Aq{sq_text}\e\*(Aq       /* left\-truncated quoted string (suffix symbol) */
\& 
\& "*"{symbol_text}"*"    /* dual\-truncated bare string (infix symbol) */
\&    {symbol_text}"*"    /* right\-truncated bare string (prefix symbol) */
\& "*"{symbol_text}       /* left\-truncated bare string (suffix symbol) */
.Ve
.PP
Truncated symbols (for
prefix\-,
suffix\-,
and
infix-queries)
are supported directly by the scanner, in order to distinguish
these from literal symbols containing an asterisk character (\*(L"*\*(R").
Literal asterisks must be escaped if they occur anywhere
in a literal symbol, e.g. by enclosing the symbol in single quotes.
Note that despite this restriction, the asterisk does \s-1NOT\s0 function as a general
\&\*(L"wildcard character\*(R" for \s-1DDC\s0 queries.  If you need to match multiple substrings of a single index
item, use a regular expression instead,
e.g. \*(L"/^foo.*bar.*baz$/\*(R" for a wildcard condition \*(L"foo*bar*baz\*(R".
.PP
\fITerm Expander Pipelines\fR
.IX Subsection "Term Expander Pipelines"
.PP
.Vb 3
\& "|"{ws}*"\-"                    /* alias for default term expander pipeline (index\-dependent) */
\& "|"{ws}*\e\*(Aq{sq_text}\e\*(Aq          /* quoted term expander label */
\& "|"{ws}*{symbol_text}          /* bare term expander label */
.Ve
.PP
The scanner supports special rules for user specification of term expansion pipelines
used by the qw_bareword and qw_set_infl
query types.  Each link in a term expansion pipeline is prefixed by the special symbol
\&\*(L"|\*(R" (vertical bar or 'pipe' symbol), followed by optional whitespace and the label of
a named expander to apply as a symbol.  In order for the
query to be evaluated, each expander label in a term expansion pipeline must be defined
for the corpus to be queried.  The expanders \*(L"id\*(R", \*(L"null\*(R", \*(L"case\*(R", and \*(L"infl\*(R"
should always be defined.  The default expanders may be overridden and/or additional
expanders defined in a corpus .opt file.
The special label \*(L"\-\*(R" (hyphen) may be used as an alias for the default expander
for the index to be queried, whose label is identical to the long index name as
declared in the corpus .opt file.  By default, only
the \*(L"Token\*(R" index has a pre-defined expansion pipeline, defined as 'infl' (built-in
language-dependent lemmatization and re-inflection) by default.
If the CaseInsensitive flag is set in the corpus .opt file,
the default Token pipeline is 'infl|case' (inflection followed by built-in letter-case twiddling).
The default expansion pipeline for any other other index is empty, i.e. equivalent to
the identity expander \*(L"id\*(R" a.k.a. \*(L"null\*(R".
Literal pipe symbols (\*(L"|\*(R") must be escaped if they occur anywhere
in a literal symbol, e.g. by enclosing the symbol in single quotes.
.PP
\fIOther Terminals\fR
.IX Subsection "Other Terminals"
.PP
.Vb 3
\& {ws}+                          /* whitespace: skip */
\& \e0                             /* null byte: skip */
\& .                              /* any other character (byte) is its own token */ }
.Ve
.PP
Whitespace and \s-1NUL\s0 bytes are ignored.
Any other input byte is returned as a symbol of length 1.
.SS "Miscellany"
.IX Subsection "Miscellany"
\fICompilation Errors\fR
.IX Subsection "Compilation Errors"
.PP
Not all queries which are grammatical according to the
query grammar given above are in fact
admissible \s-1DDC\s0 queries.  In particular, pure negative conditions
such as
!foo,
!foo && !bar,
or
!(foo || bar)
will parse successfully but fail to compile.  In such cases,
\&\s-1DDC\s0 should return an error code of errParseError
and print an informative diagnostic message to stderr
and/or the current log file.
.SS "\s-1DTA\s0 Corpus Structure"
.IX Subsection "DTA Corpus Structure"
This section gives a brief overview of the index structure used for the
current \s-1DDC\s0 index of the Deutsches Textarchiv corpus.
.PP
\fI\s-1DTA\s0 Index Fields\fR
.IX Subsection "DTA Index Fields"
.PP
The \s-1DTA\s0 corpus .opt file
defines the following index fields:
.IP "\fBToken w\fR" 4
.IX Item "Token w"
\&\fBunicruft\fR (<http://odo.dwds.de/~moocow/software/unicruft/>)Latin\-1 approximation of
original token text (actually encoded in the Latin\-1 subset of \s-1UTF\-8\s0).
This is the default field searched e.g. by bareword \s-1SYMBOL\s0queries.
As of August, 2011, words containing non-latin-extended characters are \fBnot\fRtransliterated by default, and should appear (and be searchable) by their original \s-1UTF\-8\s0 forms
without resorting to the \*(L"Utf8\*(R" index field (with regard to which see below).
.IP "\fBUtf8 u\fR" 4
.IX Item "Utf8 u"
Original \s-1UTF\-8\s0 text of the source token.  Formerly indexed as \fIToken2 w2\fR.
.IP "\fBCanonicalToken v\fR" 4
.IX Item "CanonicalToken v"
\&\fB\s-1DTA::CAB\s0\fR (http://odo.dwds.de/~moocow/software/dta\-cab/ <http://odo.dwds.de/~moocow/software/dta-cab/>)\-normalized wordform for the source token.
.IP "\fBPos p\fR" 4
.IX Item "Pos p"
Part-of-speech assigned to the source token
by \fBmoot\fR (http://www.ling.uni\-potsdam.de/~moocow/projects/moot/ <http://www.ling.uni-potsdam.de/~moocow/projects/moot/>)via \fB\s-1DTA::CAB\s0\fR (http://odo.dwds.de/~moocow/software/dta\-cab/ <http://odo.dwds.de/~moocow/software/dta-cab/>).
Uses the \fB\s-1STTS\s0 tag-set\fR (http://www.ims.uni\-stuttgart.de/projekte/corplex/TagSets/stts\-table.html <http://www.ims.uni-stuttgart.de/projekte/corplex/TagSets/stts-table.html>).
.IP "\fBLemma l\fR" 4
.IX Item "Lemma l"
Lemma assigned to the source token by \fB\s-1DTA::CAB\s0\fR (http://odo.dwds.de/~moocow/software/dta\-cab/ <http://odo.dwds.de/~moocow/software/dta-cab/>).
Uses the \fB\s-1TAGH\s0 morphology\fR (<http://tagh.de/>)via \fB\s-1DTA::CAB\s0\fR (http://odo.dwds.de/~moocow/software/dta\-cab/ <http://odo.dwds.de/~moocow/software/dta-cab/>)if available.
.IP "\fBCoord coord\fR" 4
.IX Item "Coord coord"
Bounding box(es) for the source token.
Not really meaningful for querying, but useful for image highlighting.
.IP "\fBPage page\fR" 4
.IX Item "Page page"
Page (scan) number.
Formerly used the long index name \*(L"age\*(R", which appears to have been nothing more than
a self-perpetuating typographical error.
.IP "\fBRend r\fR" 4
.IX Item "Rend r"
Typographical (\*(L"rendition\*(R") attributes for the source token as as '|'\-sparated set
e.g. \*(L"\-\*(R" (nothing of note), \*(L"|aq|\*(R" (antiqua), \*(L"|b|\*(R" (bold?), \*(L"|g|\*(R" (upper-case?),
\&\*(L"|b|g|\*(R" (bold? + upper-case?), ...
.IP "\fBContext con\fR" 4
.IX Item "Context con"
Text-structurual features of the source token as a lexicographically sorted
\&'|'\-separated list of unique structural properties,
or \*(L"\-\*(R" if the token has no special text-structural properties at all.
Supported properties inherited from \s-1XML\s0 ancestor elements are:
\&\f(CW\*(C`text, front, body, back, head, left, foot, end, argument, hi, cit, fw, lg, stage, speaker, formula,\*(C'\fRand \f(CW\*(C`table\*(C'\fR.
Additionally, the properties
\&\f(CW\*(C`note_foot, note_left, note_right\*(C'\fRand \f(CW\*(C`note_other\*(C'\fRare used for tokens with an \s-1XML\s0 \f(CW\*(C`note\*(C'\fRancestor.
.IP "\fBXPath xpath\fR" 4
.IX Item "XPath xpath"
XPath to the deepest element node containing (the first character of) the current token,
or \*(L"\-\*(R" if no such XPath was available during indexing.
Note that any prefix \*(L"/TEI/text\*(R" or \*(L"/TEI\*(R" is implicitly trimmed from the indexed XPath strings,
since all ddc-indexed tokens must occur as descendants of a /TEI/text element.
.IP "\fBLine lb\fR" 4
.IX Item "Line lb"
Line number of the current token, relative to the
current page as indexed by the \fBpage\fRfield.
Defined as the number of opening (and possibly closing) "\f(CW\*(C`lb\*(C'\fR\*(L"
preceding the first character of the current token
on the current page; e.g. 0 (zero) if no \*(R"\f(CW\*(C`lb\*(C'\fR" elements precede
the first character of the current token on the current page.
Precedence and page-association are computed in terms of \s-1TEI\s0 document order;
e.g. if chapter headings contain \f(CW\*(C`lb\*(C'\fRelements, these will count
towards the line number assigned.
.PP
\fI\s-1DTA\s0 Term Expanders\fR
.IX Subsection "DTA Term Expanders"
.PP
The \s-1DTA\s0 corpus .opt file
defines the following term expanders:
.IP "\fBid\fR" 4
.IX Item "id"
Identity expander (no-op)
.IP "\fBnull\fR" 4
.IX Item "null"
Identity expander (no-op)
.IP "\fBcase\fR" 4
.IX Item "case"
Case-twiddling expander using current locale settings of the running server process,
which should have an \s-1LC_CTYPE\s0 character set of \*(L"\s-1UTF\-8\s0\*(R" or equivalent for correct results.
Not used by default.
.IP "\fBtolower\fR" 4
.IX Item "tolower"
.PD 0
.IP "\fBlc\fR" 4
.IX Item "lc"
.PD
Case-twiddling expander which forces input to all lower-case.
Same caveats as for the caseexpander.
Not used by default.
.IP "\fBtoupper\fR" 4
.IX Item "toupper"
.PD 0
.IP "\fBuc\fR" 4
.IX Item "uc"
.PD
Case-twiddling expander which forces input to all upper-case.
Same caveats as for the caseexpander.
Not used by default.
.IP "\fBmorphy\fR" 4
.IX Item "morphy"
Built-in \s-1DDC\s0 lemmatization and re-inflection (morphy-based)
.IP "\fBinfl\fR" 4
.IX Item "infl"
.PD 0
.IP "\fBtagh\fR" 4
.IX Item "tagh"
.PD
TAGH-based lemmatization and re-inflection via dedicated
\&\fB\s-1DTA::CAB\s0\fR (http://odo.dwds.de/~moocow/software/dta\-cab/ <http://odo.dwds.de/~moocow/software/dta-cab/>)HTTP server
at \fBhttp://194.95.188.28:9098\fR (<http://194.95.188.28:9098>).
.IP "\fBcab\fR" 4
.IX Item "cab"
Expansion by an external \fB\s-1DTA::CAB\s0\fR (http://odo.dwds.de/~moocow/software/dta\-cab/ <http://odo.dwds.de/~moocow/software/dta-cab/>)HTTP server at
\&\fBhttp://194.95.188.36:9099\fR (<http://194.95.188.36:9099>)using the \*(L"expand\*(R" analyzer method (phonetic and rewrite equivalents).
.IP "\fBpho\fR" 4
.IX Item "pho"
Expansion by the external \s-1DTA::CAB\s0 \s-1HTTP\s0 server at
using only the \*(L"eqpho\*(R" analyzer method (phonetic equivalents only).
.IP "\fBrw\fR" 4
.IX Item "rw"
Expansion by the external \s-1DTA::CAB\s0 \s-1HTTP\s0 server at
using only the \*(L"eqrw\*(R" analyzer method (rewrite equivalents only).
Should be more precise than the
cabor phoexpanders, but with poorer recall.
.IP "\fBeqlemma\fR" 4
.IX Item "eqlemma"
TAGH-based best-lemma match using pre-compiled index via
via dedicated \fB\s-1DTA::CAB\s0\fR (http://odo.dwds.de/~moocow/software/dta\-cab/ <http://odo.dwds.de/~moocow/software/dta-cab/>)HTTP server
at \fBhttp://194.95.188.36:9099\fR (<http://194.95.188.36:9099>).
.IP "\fBToken\fR" 4
.IX Item "Token"
Default expansion pipeline for queries of the (transliterated) 'Token' index,
defined as 
\&\f(CW\*(C`eqlemma\*(C'\fR.
.IP "\fBUtf8\fR" 4
.IX Item "Utf8"
Default expansion pipeline for queries of the (raw \s-1UTF\-8\s0) 'Utf8' index,
defined as 
\&\f(CW\*(C`eqlemma\*(C'\fR.
Note that due to limitations and configuration issues with respect to both the underlying \s-1CAB\s0 server
and the built-in \s-1DDC\s0 morphological expansion module,
target strings containing extinct characters
(\*(L"ſ\*(R", \*(L"aͤ\*(R", etc.) will \fBnot\fRbe found by this expander.
.IP "\fBCanonicalToken\fR" 4
.IX Item "CanonicalToken"
Default expansion pipeline for queries of the CAB-normalized 'CanonicalToken' index,
defined as 
\&\f(CW\*(C`infl\*(C'\fR.
.IP "\fBPos\fR" 4
.IX Item "Pos"
Default expansion pipeline for queries of the 'Pos' (part-of-speech tag) index,
defined as 
\&\f(CW\*(C`toupper\*(C'\fR.
.IP "\fBLemma\fR" 4
.IX Item "Lemma"
Default expansion pipeline for queries of the 'Lemma',
defined as 
\&\f(CW\*(C`case\*(C'\fR.
.SS "Examples"
.IX Subsection "Examples"
The examples in this section assume the \s-1DTA\s0 \s-1DDC\s0 corpus index structure
described above.
The links in this section make use of the \s-1DTA\s0 OpenSearch wrapper
demo server at
http://kaskade.dwds.de/dtaos.
.PP
\fIBasic Examples\fR
.IX Subsection "Basic Examples"
.IP "\fBsein\fR" 4
.IX Item "sein"
All expanded variants of \*(L"sein\*(R" (\*(L"sein\*(R", \*(L"ist\*(R", \*(L"war\*(R", ..., \*(L"seyn\*(R", \*(L"seyd\*(R", ..., \*(L"seine\*(R", \*(L"ihre\*(R", ...)
.ie n .IP "\fB\fB@sein\fB\fR" 4
.el .IP "\fB\f(CB@sein\fB\fR" 4
.IX Item "@sein"
Only the literal (latin\-1 approximation) string \*(L"sein\*(R"
.ie n .IP "\fB\fB$u\fB=@ſein\fR" 4
.el .IP "\fB\f(CB$u\fB=@ſein\fR" 4
.IX Item "$u=@ſein"
Only the literal (original \s-1UTF\-8\s0) string \*(L"ſein\*(R"
.IP "\fBWach*\fR" 4
.IX Item "Wach*"
Any string with (latin\-1 approximation) prefix \*(L"Wach\*(R"
.IP "\fB*stube\fR" 4
.IX Item "*stube"
Any string with (latin\-1 approximation) suffix \*(L"stube\*(R"
.IP "\fB*achs*\fR" 4
.IX Item "*achs*"
Any string with (latin\-1 approximation) substring \*(L"achs\*(R"
.ie n .IP "\fB\fB$u\fB=/ſtube$/\fR" 4
.el .IP "\fB\f(CB$u\fB=/ſtube$/\fR" 4
.IX Item "$u=/ſtube$/"
Any string with (original \s-1UTF\-8\s0) suffix \*(L"ſtube\*(R" (via regex)
.ie n .IP "\fB\fB$u\fB=/ſtube$/i\fR" 4
.el .IP "\fB\f(CB$u\fB=/ſtube$/i\fR" 4
.IX Item "$u=/ſtube$/i"
Any string with (original \s-1UTF\-8\s0) suffix \*(L"ſtube\*(R" (via regex, case-insensitve)
.PP
\fITerm Expansion Examples\fR
.IX Subsection "Term Expansion Examples"
.IP "\fBTür\fR" 4
.IX Item "Tür"
All sentences containing any variant of the word 'Tür'
.ie n .IP "\fB\fB$Token\fB=Tür\fR" 4
.el .IP "\fB\f(CB$Token\fB=Tür\fR" 4
.IX Item "$Token=Tür"
\&... same condition, with explicit index
.ie n .IP "\fB\fB$Token\fB=Tür |Token\fR" 4
.el .IP "\fB\f(CB$Token\fB=Tür |Token\fR" 4
.IX Item "$Token=Tür |Token"
\&... same condition, with explicit index and expansion pipeline
.IP "\fBTür |Token\fR" 4
.IX Item "Tür |Token"
\&... same condition, with explicit expansion pipeline only
.IP "\fBTür |\-\fR" 4
.IX Item "Tür |-"
\&... same condition, with \*(L"\-\*(R" expansion pipeline alias
.IP "\fBTür |infl|cab\fR" 4
.IX Item "Tür |infl|cab"
\&... same condition, with alternative user expansion pipeline
.IP "\fBTür |infl\fR" 4
.IX Item "Tür |infl"
All (modern) inflectional variants of the word \*(L"Tür\*(R" (no \s-1CAB\s0 expansion)
.IP "\fBTür |cab\fR" 4
.IX Item "Tür |cab"
All graphematic variants of the form \*(L"Tür\*(R" (no lemmatization or re-inflection)
.IP "\fBTür |case\fR" 4
.IX Item "Tür |case"
All letter-case variants of the form \*(L"Tür\*(R"
.IP "\fBTür |infl|case\fR" 4
.IX Item "Tür |infl|case"
All letter-case variants of any modern inflectional variant of the word \*(L"Tür\*(R"
.IP "\fBTür |pho\fR" 4
.IX Item "Tür |pho"
All phonetic variants of the form \*(L"Tür\*(R"
.IP "\fBTür |rw\fR" 4
.IX Item "Tür |rw"
All rewrite variants of the form \*(L"Tür\*(R"
.IP "\fBTür |infl|rw\fR" 4
.IX Item "Tür |infl|rw"
All rewrite variants of any modern inflectional variant of the word \*(L"Tür\*(R"
.PP
\fIMulti-Token Examples\fR
.IX Subsection "Multi-Token Examples"
.IP "\fBVerein && Club\fR" 4
.IX Item "Verein && Club"
All sentences containing both 'Verein' and 'Club' (variants)
.IP "\fBVerein || Club\fR" 4
.IX Item "Verein || Club"
All sentences containing either 'Verein' or 'Club' (variants)
.IP "\fB{Verein,Club}\fR" 4
.IX Item "{Verein,Club}"
\&... the same condition, in set notation
.ie n .IP "\fB\fB@Verein\fB || \f(BI@Club\fB\fR" 4
.el .IP "\fB\f(CB@Verein\fB || \f(CB@Club\fB\fR" 4
.IX Item "@Verein || @Club"
All sentences containing either 'Verein' or 'Club' (literals)
.IP "\fB@{Verein,Club}\fR" 4
.IX Item "@{Verein,Club}"
\&... the same condition, in set notation
.IP "\fB*{verein,club}\fR" 4
.IX Item "*{verein,club}"
All strings ending in either \*(L"verein\*(R" or \*(L"club\*(R"
.IP "\fB/(?:\eQverein\eE|\eQclub\eE)$/\fR" 4
.IX Item "/(?:QvereinE|QclubE)$/"
\&... the same condition, in regex notation
.IP "\fB/(?:\eQverein\eE|\eQclub\eE)$/i\fR" 4
.IX Item "/(?:QvereinE|QclubE)$/i"
\&... case-insensitive (includes e.g. \*(L"Verein\*(R" and \*(L"Club\*(R")
.ie n .IP "\fB""ein Verein""\fR" 4
.el .IP "\fB``ein Verein''\fR" 4
.IX Item "ein Verein"
All variants of the substring \*(L"ein Verein\*(R"
.ie n .IP "\fB""@ein \fB@Verein\fB""\fR" 4
.el .IP "\fB``@ein \f(CB@Verein\fB''\fR" 4
.IX Item "@ein @Verein"
The exact substring \*(L"ein Verein\*(R"
.ie n .IP "\fB""ein #1 Verein""\fR" 4
.el .IP "\fB``ein #1 Verein''\fR" 4
.IX Item "ein #1 Verein"
All variants of the subsequence \*(L"ein Verein\*(R" with at most 1 intervening word
.ie n .IP "\fB""ein #1 {Verein,Club}""\fR" 4
.el .IP "\fB``ein #1 {Verein,Club}''\fR" 4
.IX Item "ein #1 {Verein,Club}"
All variants of one of the substrings \*(L"ein Verein\*(R" or \*(L"ein Club\*(R" with at most 1 intervening word
.PP
\fIQuery Filter Examples\fR
.IX Subsection "Query Filter Examples"
.IP "\fBMax\fR" 4
.IX Item "Max"
All sentences containing a variant of \*(L"Max\*(R", unsorted
.IP "\fBMax #has_field[author,/Busch/]\fR" 4
.IX Item "Max #has_field[author,/Busch/]"
\&... only those documents by an author matching the regex \f(CW\*(C`/Busch/\*(C'\fR
.IP "\fBMax #has[author,/busch/i]\fR" 4
.IX Item "Max #has[author,/busch/i]"
\&... same condition, using new \f(CW\*(C`#has\*(C'\fRalias for \f(CW\*(C`#has_field\*(C'\fRand case-insensitive regex
.IP "\fBMax #less_by[author]\fR" 4
.IX Item "Max #less_by[author]"
\&... sorted in ascending order by author string
.IP "\fBMax #greater_by_rank\fR" 4
.IX Item "Max #greater_by_rank"
\&... sorted in descending order by putative relevance
.IP "\fBMax #less_by_size\fR" 4
.IX Item "Max #less_by_size"
\&... sorted in ascending order by hit (sentence) length
.IP "\fBMax #less_by_size[3,5]\fR" 4
.IX Item "Max #less_by_size[3,5]"
\&... sorted in ascending order by hit length, where hit length is between 3 and 4 tokens.
.IP "\fBMax #less_by_date\fR" 4
.IX Item "Max #less_by_date"
\&... sorted in ascending order by hit date
.IP "\fBMax #date[1865]\fR" 4
.IX Item "Max #date[1865]"
\&... only those hits from 1865
